✓ LongMemEval-M full-haystack, full engine (spine-sort + per-topic consolidation ledgers + dream-tier retrieval) — multi-session category
  dataset: LongMemEval-M · full-haystack (~480 distractor sessions per question)
  answer model: gemini-2.5-pro · judge: gemini-2.5-flash (flexible)
  recomputed from 8 published rows: 5/8 = 62.5%
  claimed headline:                        5/8 = 62.5%
  match: total ok · hits ok · accuracy ok
  per-category:
    multi-session              5/8
  replay rule: 2 first-run HIT(s) did NOT reproduce → scored MISS:
    gpt4_59c863d7    judge noise (false positive). The engine gave the SAME answer — 6 kits — in both runs; the ground truth is five. The first run's judge scored it HIT, the replay scored it MISS. Scored MISS here per the replay rule.
    aae3761f         answer variance (not judge noise). The first run answered 15 hours and was correctly scored HIT; the replay answered 11 hours — it found only two of the three trips — and was correctly scored MISS. The verdict did not reproduce, so it is scored MISS here per the replay rule.
  scope: THIS LEDGER COVERS ONLY THE MULTI-SESSION CATEGORY (8 of the 48 questions). The other 40 questions were never re-run with the engine — see composition_note.

